From: OE-Alliance <oe-alliance@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: use receiver EXIT as back while the menu is open

The udev driver normalizes KEY_EXIT to RETROK_CLEAR. Our launcher binds
this to menu_toggle, which cannot pop a submenu and does nothing without
running content. Translate this keyboard hotkey to the menu's cancel
button while the menu is alive; keep its existing toggle action in-game.

Do this on the collected input state, not the evdev key events: changing
the key translation when the menu opens would mismatch press/release and
could leave a key stuck. The normal menu input flushing and edge detection
handle held keys. Respect swapped confirm/cancel buttons and dismiss the
on-screen keyboard using its existing Select action. Gamepad menu combos
are added later by the runloop and are not changed.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [receiver remote-control policy]

--- a/input/input_driver.c
+++ b/input/input_driver.c
@@ -6922,6 +6922,34 @@ void input_driver_collect_system_input(input_driver_state_t *input_st,
    }
 
 #ifdef HAVE_MENU
+#ifdef HAVE_UDEV
+   /* Receiver EXIT opens the menu in-game, but goes back inside it. */
+   if (     menu_is_alive
+         && current_input
+         && current_input->input_state
+         && string_is_equal(current_input->ident, "udev")
+         && input_config_binds[0][RARCH_MENU_TOGGLE].key == RETROK_CLEAR
+         && current_input->input_state(
+               input_st->current_data,
+               joypad,
+               sec_joypad,
+               &joypad_info,
+               (const retro_keybind_set *)input_config_binds,
+               (input_st->flags & INP_FLAG_KB_MAPPING_BLOCKED) ? true : false,
+               0,
+               RETRO_DEVICE_KEYBOARD, 0, RETROK_CLEAR))
+   {
+      unsigned cancel_btn = settings->bools.input_menu_swap_ok_cancel_buttons
+            ? RETRO_DEVICE_ID_JOYPAD_A : RETRO_DEVICE_ID_JOYPAD_B;
+
+      BIT256_CLEAR_PTR(current_bits, RARCH_MENU_TOGGLE);
+      if (display_kb)
+         BIT256_SET_PTR(current_bits, RETRO_DEVICE_ID_JOYPAD_SELECT);
+      else
+         BIT256_SET_PTR(current_bits, cancel_btn);
+   }
+#endif /* HAVE_UDEV */
+
    if (menu_input_active)
    {
       /* Gather keyboard input, if enabled
